#opener("This chapter will help you unpack your Macintosh PiForma, set up its traveling companions, and start the computer. You will also learn how to check a reluctant battery, shut down properly, and return everything to the bag. The packing order is worth a little attention. The foam has opinions.")
#heading(level:2,"Unpacking the equipment")
#para([#text("Set the carrying bag upright on a stable surface and open it. Leave room nearby for each item as you take it out.")])
#instruction(1,[#strong[#text("Remove the small brown accessory pouch near the top.")] #text("It contains two Nintendo 64 controllers, the USB hub, and the power cable. Set the pouch and its contents aside.")])
#instruction(2,[#strong[#text("Take out the mouse and the collapsible computer stand beneath the pouch.")]])
#instruction(3,[#strong[#text("Remove this printed guide.")] #text("If you are reading it, you have already done this step. Well done.")])
#instruction(4,[#strong[#text("Lift out the mouse pad beneath the guide.")]])
#instruction(5,[#strong[#text("Remove the velvet-covered foam board beneath the mouse pad.")] #text("Keep it flat; it protects the computer when everything is packed.")])
#para([#text("The PiForma is underneath the board, with its monitor/screen facing upward. The keyboard is tucked against one side of the computer. It is not another layer in the stack. Note which way it faces, as described under “The keyboard’s place” below, and lift the keyboard out first, before the computer.")])
#para([#text("Lift the PiForma by its handle and case. Do not push on the screen: pressing on the display can damage the screen or its mounts.")])
#illustration-plate("1-1", "bag-arrangement.png", "Arrangement in the carrying bag. The printed guide is not shown; it lies beneath the mouse and stand, above the mouse pad.", width:320.000pt)
#subhead("Finding the handle")
#para([#text("The carrying handle may be hidden against the inside front wall of the bag. Slide a hand down inside that wall, along the top side of the PiForma, until you can pull the handle outward. Do not pull on a connector or an edge of the display to lift the machine.")])
#para([#text("If lifting it out upright is awkward, lay the bag on its back first and try the gentler removal angle. Lift carefully. There is no prize for wrestling it out upright.")])
#subhead("The keyboard’s place")
#para([#text("Notice the keyboard’s orientation before moving it: the keys face the bag wall, the thicker edge faces the rear of the bag, and the thinner edge faces the front. Remember these three directions when you pack it again.")])
#para([#text("The molded edges in the bottom foam locate the rear/bottom of the computer. The first photograph shows the empty base; the second shows the PiForma and keyboard in place. Match the keyboard's orientation, rather than merely finding a gap large enough to hold it.")])
