#heading(level:2,"Your first session")
#para([#text("Once the desktop appears, try this short tour. You need not change any settings or make a file.")])
#screen-figure("1-7","piforma-desktop-overview.svg","The PiForma desktop: persistent system menu bar across the top, AtEase in the center, Control Strip at lower left, and Clippy at lower right.",width:366pt)
#instruction(1,[#strong[#text("Move the mouse on its pad and watch the pointer follow it.")] #text("Point at an item by moving the pointer over it. To click, press and release the left mouse button once. The other left button can wait for Chapter 3.")])
#instruction(2,[#strong[#text("Find the menu bar at the top of the screen and the folder-like AtEase launcher beneath it.")] #text("If a window covers the launcher, choose View → Show Desktop from the top menu bar. This reveals the desktop without quitting your programs.")])
#instruction(3,[#strong[#text("In AtEase, click a folder tab if needed, then click a program button once.")] #text("Wait for its window to appear before clicking again. Use a windowed program for this first exercise; a full-screen game will cover the desktop.")])
#instruction(4,[#strong[#text("Explore the program's visible controls.")] #text("When finished, use its own Quit or Exit command if it has one, or its window close control. If asked to save something you want to keep, save it before continuing. Closing one window may leave other windows from the same program open.")])
#instruction(5,[#strong[#text("Choose View → Show Desktop to return to the launcher.")] #text("You can now open another program in the same way.")])
#para([#text("For a small practice window with a known menu entry, choose Apple menu → About This PiForma. Read the information, close that window using its close control, and return to AtEase. Opening a program, leaving it, and finding your way back are most of the battle. Chapter 3 explains windows, typing, files and games in more detail.")])
#screen-figure("1-8","piforma-about-system.svg","Apple menu → About This PiForma opens the information window. The figures shown describe that running session, rather than fixed memory-use specifications.",width:366pt)
#para([#text("The About window is not the project guide. To read the guide itself, click PiForma Guide in AtEase; Chapter 3 describes it.")])
#para([#text("If the launcher or menu bar is missing, see Appendix B rather than trying unfamiliar touch gestures. When you have finished using the computer, follow “Stopping the computer” below.")])
#heading(level:2,"Stopping the computer")
#instruction(1,[#strong[#text("Save your work and leave any game or application using its own quit command when available.")]])
#instruction(2,[#strong[#text("In the PiForma Panel menu bar, choose Special → Shut Down.")]])
#instruction(3,[#strong[#text("If a confirmation appears, choose Shut Down.")] #text("Let the operating system finish shutting down before removing physical power. A blank screen alone can also mean the display is asleep, so do not use darkness as the only confirmation.")])
#instruction(4,[#strong[#text("Once shutdown is complete, turn off the right-side physical power control.")] #text("The wiring permits battery charging while this control is off.")])
#screen-figure("1-9","piforma-shutdown-menu.svg","Choose Special → Shut Down after saving your work. This view shows the menu choice, not completed shutdown.",width:242pt)
#para([#text("The physical power switch can cut the computer’s power. Reserve an abrupt power-off for a last resort when the system will not respond, rather than treating it as the normal way to stop. It can lose unsaved work or damage files.")])
#para([#text("To leave a full-screen program rather than stop the computer, see “Leaving a full-screen program” in Chapter 3. A hold of about six seconds closes only the active application on the current PiForma.")])
#heading(level:2,"Packing the equipment")
#instruction(1,[#strong[#text("Shut down properly, switch off physical power, and disconnect external cables as needed.")] #text("Make sure the computer and accessories are cool and dry before putting them away.")])
#instruction(2,[#strong[#text("Place the PiForma in the bag with its monitor/screen facing upward.")] #text("Its rear/bottom must seat in the molded indents in the bottom foam insert.")])
#instruction(3,[#strong[#text("Gently shift or wiggle it into its intended resting place.")] #text("It should not move much when seated. Do not force it down or put pressure on the display.")])
#instruction(4,[#strong[#text("Put the keyboard beside the computer: keys toward the bag wall, thicker edge toward the rear, thinner edge toward the front.")]])
#instruction(5,[#strong[#text("Place the velvet-covered foam board above the computer.")]])
#instruction(6,[#strong[#text("Put the mouse pad above the board, then this guide above the pad.")]])
#instruction(7,[#strong[#text("Put the mouse and collapsible stand above the guide.")]])
#instruction(8,[#strong[#text("Return the two controllers, hub, and power cable to the brown pouch and place that pouch at the top.")] #text("Check that no loose item presses against the screen and close the bag gently.")])
#subhead("Checking the charging alignment")
#para([#text("Seating the rear/bottom in the molded foam indents aligns the bag’s wireless-charging arrangement. A hidden transmitter sits under the velvet, with its USB power cable routed into a back pocket. This is a slow, trickle-charging arrangement, not fast charging.")])
#para([#text("Physical fit does not prove that charging has started. Check the foam seating and that the charging cable in the back pocket has power. The battery display can indicate whether power from the wireless receiver is charging the battery, but the display is hidden while the computer is packed in the bag. Without a USB power monitor on the bag charger's supply, it is rather a hope-and-pray arrangement.")])
#para([#text("A USB power monitor in the bag charger's USB supply connection can show whether it is drawing power. That gives you more evidence than a hopeful glance at the bag, but it is not a direct measurement of energy reaching the battery. Do not press the computer farther into the bag in search of a better fit.")])
#subhead("Carrying the bag")
#para([#text("Lift and carry the closed bag carefully. The padding offers useful protection against ordinary handling; it does not make the computer immune to hard impacts. Cushioning is not armor. The Bose speakers and stands do not fit in this bag; carry them separately.")])
